    "lawCode": "Add §13.44, Ment Hyg L",
    "lawSection": "Mental Hygiene Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S593\n\nSPONSOR: ORTT\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to Down syndrome\ndiagnosis awareness\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo require information on Down syndrome be provided to a pregnant woman,\nparent, or expectant parent of any infant or fetus diagnosed with Down\nsyndrome.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAdd a new section 13.43 of the mental hygiene law to state that a health\ncare practitioner who orders tests of a pregnant woman or infant to\nscreen for Down syndrome shall provide information if a positive test is\nrevealed.\n\nSuch information includes up-to-date and evidence based information\nreviewed by medical experts and national Down syndrome organizations and\nmay include expected physical, developmental, education and psychosocial\noutcomes, life expectancy, clinical course description, expected intel-\nlectual and functional development, and treatment options. Information\ncan include contact information for support groups, hotlines, and other\nrelevant contact information.  This information shall be provide by the\ncommissioner in writing, and also be posted on the Office's website.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nDown syndrome is the most common genetic disease in the United States\nwith 1 in 700 babies born with this condition. Prenatal screening has\nbeen available since the 1970's. This legislation seeks to provide\ninformation related to the positive outcomes the life an individual with\nDown syndrome can live. There currently is not information readily\navailable to be provided to families about the positive life outcomes\none can expect in the life of an individual with Down syndrome.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-2022: S. 2163 Referred to Mental Health\n\nS.197 of 2019-20, Referred to Mental Health and Developmental Disabili-\nties S.7345 of\n\n2018, Advanced to Third Reading.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day.\n",
